# Binary Tree Types

## Full Binary Tree
Every node has **either 0 or 2 children**. No node has exactly 1 child.

## Complete Binary Tree
All levels are **completely filled except the last level**, and the last level has nodes as far **left** as possible.

## Perfect Binary Tree
All **leaf nodes are at the same level**. Every internal node has exactly 2 children.

## Balanced Binary Tree
Height of the tree is at most **O(log n)**, where n = number of nodes.
Used in: AVL Trees, Red-Black Trees.

